nteraction energy shows the -7/3 power law ; this is understood through the scaling analysis for the hydrodynamic equations of spins and confirmed by the numerical simulation of the gp equations . furthermore , the spin density vectors are spatially random but temporally frozen , which reminds us of the analogy with spin glass ; the order parameter certainly grows in st . however , the story is just more complicated when the interaction is antiferromagnetic . then appears a boundary wave number @xmath102 , and the scaling analysis in st finds that the energy spectrum obeys the -1 power law for @xmath92 and the -7/3 law for @xmath94 ; the -7/3 power law was confirmed numerically . this energy spectrum actually comes from the small spin amplitude due to the antiferromagnetic interaction . the similar situation is expected to occur also for the ferromagnetic system under a static magnetic field that reduces the spin amplitude , in which both -1 and -7/3 power laws were confirmed clearly by the numerical simulation . the spin - glass - like behavior did not appear in the antiferromagnetic st . such a spin - disordered state was experimentally created in a trapped system through the instability of the initial helical structures of spin , and actually observed @xcite . creating st and observing the spin density vector @xmath103 would allow us to investigate the energy spectrum @xmath63 and the spin - glass - like behavior . it is very important to ask what causes the energy cascade in st . a mechanism causing the kolmogorov @xmath104 power law in classical turbulences is considered to be the richardson cascade of vortices @xcite . since there are very few topological defects in our simulation of st , however , the cascade due to them is not relevant . at present we guess the cascade of spin waves plays an important role for st . this will be worked in reference to the wave turbulence theory @xcite . usual selfsimilar power law in the inertial range of turbulence is caused by some dissipation at high wave numbers , which makes the energy flow towards high wave numbers . our system based on eq . ( [ 2dgp ] ) conserves the total energy ; no dissipative mechanisms are included in our formulation . thus it is not so trivial to understand why and how the characteristic power laws are built and sustained in @xmath63 . here we should note that spinor becs have superfluid degrees of freedom ( mass current ) as well as spin degrees of freedom and they are coupled . hence the spin - dependent interaction energy @xmath105 is not conserved in the dynamics . while spin develops st , superfluid may create its own turbulence . it would be quite interesting to investigate how these degrees of freedom interact with each other and develop turbulence for the whole system . the authors thank yusuke aoki for the scientific collaboration and the preparation of the manuscript . 99 halperin w p and tsubota m ( eds ) 2009 _ progress in low temperature physics _ ( amsterdam : elsevier ) fetter a l 2009 _ rev . * 81 * 647 kasamatsu k. and tsubota m 2009 _ prog . low temp . halperin w p and tsubota m vol  16 ( amsterdam : elsevier ) p  351 fetter a l 2010 _ j. low temp . phys . _ * 161 * 445 anderson b p 2010 _ j. low temp . phys . _ * 161 * 574 berloff n g and svistunov b 2002 _ phys . rev . _ a * 66 * 013603 parker n g and adams c s 2005 _ phys . lett . _ * 95 * 145301 kobayashi m and tsubota m 2007 _ phys . rev . _ a * 76 * 045603 henn e a l , seman j a , ramos e r f , caracanhas m , castilho p , olmpio e p , roati g , magalhes d v , magalhes k m f and bagnato v s 2009 _ phys . rev . _ a * 79 * 043618 henn e a l , seman j a , roati g , magalhes k m f and bagnato v s 2009 _ phys . rev . * 103 * 045301 kasamatsu k , tsubota m and ueda m 2005 _ int . phys._b * 19 * 1835 kawaguchi y and ueda m 2013 _ phys . rep . _ * 520 * 253 stamper - kurn d m and ueda m 2013 _ rev . phys . _ * 85 * 1191 tsubota m , kasamatsu k and kobayashi m 2013 _ novel superfluids _ ed . b